			"notes": "## DSC 1.1.13 — Fix Incremental Persistence Crashes\n\nFixes a `ConcurrentModificationException` in 1.1.12 that could crash the server during incremental storage saves and cause shutdown saving to fail again.\n\n### Fixes\n- Fixed snapshot cursor invalidation after a provisional item variant is inserted and rolled back, including simulated insertions and failed hopper transfers.\n- Added structural version tracking separate from committed content versions, allowing snapshot cursors to restart before accessing an invalid iterator.\n- Added defensive recovery that discards partial snapshots after unexpected iterator failures.\n- Rebuild pending snapshots during final flush and shutdown instead of reusing previously retained cursors.\n\n### Validation\n- Reproduced the original crash with a regression test before applying the fix.\n- Added coverage for transaction commit/rollback, simulated insertion, nested hopper rollback, snapshot budgets, recovery, and persistence round trips.\n- Passed the complete built-in self-test, integration diagnostics, and standalone server verification using the final release JAR, including normal shutdown saving."
